WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Internal bleeding is one of the most challenging situations you might face because unlike a cut or a scrape the danger is hidden beneath the skin.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:14.440
Since you can't see the hemorrhage directly you have to rely on your assessment of the situation to know when something is wrong.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:21.240
You should always suspect internal bleeding if someone has been involved in a high-impact event such as a car accident, a

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.639
significant fall, or a hard hit during a contact sport.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.520
Because the bleeding is inside the signs can be subtle at first.

00:00:28.639 --> 00:00:30.639
You're looking for things like bruising,

00:00:30.639 --> 00:00:37.720
shortness of breath, or complaints of intense pain in the chest or abdomen. If you feel the person's abdomen and the tissue feels

00:00:37.959 --> 00:00:43.320
unusually hard or if they begin vomiting or coughing up blood those are major red flags.

00:00:43.599 --> 00:00:48.700
You might also notice if the person is beginning to show signs of shock such as appearing pale,

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:55.099
cold, or confused. The most important thing to remember is that you cannot fix internal bleeding in the field.

00:00:55.099 --> 00:01:00.500
It requires a hospital and professional care. Your priority is to call 9-1-1 immediately.

00:01:01.299 --> 00:01:05.779
While you wait for EMS to arrive your secondary task is to control any

00:01:06.019 --> 00:01:11.900
external bleeding you can see to prevent further blood loss and keep the person as calm and still as possible.

